  "limitations": [
    "Original exterior of the current five-arch Ponte alle Grazie from three actually inspected ordinary side/oblique pictures and retained exact map controls. No downloaded mesh,private photo texture,bespoke architectural/terrain survey or archive research. The medieval bridge,traffic,exact public artworks,signs,graffiti,village/city buildings,full native quay walls and submerged foundations are outside scope.",
    "The exact OSM/Q2517000 bridge envelope is140.852m long,about15.6m across the main deck and19.87m across cutwater projections. It is not forced to the rounded150m reference or an unrelated reported open-span length. Paired projecting map tips establish four asymmetric pier stations and five unequal openings. Pier shaft widths,arch spring/crown/sections,deck crown and abutment construction remain photographic reconstructions,not an engineering span schedule.",
    "Each shallow concrete arch has a physically open passage across the entire deck width. Continuous exterior strip surfaces avoid overlapping internal arch-slice caps. Four warm sandstone-clad piers retain mapped pointed cutwaters up to deck level;the rail outline follows those projections. Separate road,curbed stone pavements,open metal guardrails,pier lamps and approximate dashed traffic paint are present near. Master adds dense original ashlar-block relief and paving joints;these are not replicas of individual historic stones. Far levels omit thin rails,lamps,joints and fine paving. The mapped south-end transverse crossing is represented by the authored deck and approximate bounded zebra paint;the native crossing overlay is replaced explicitly.",
    "Model datum46m and approximate9m deck rise plus0.2m crown preserve the observed proportions. The unmodified129x129/2m field oversamples one coarse ordinary global DEM tile. Foundation/abutment embedding is checked,but the field places the bank-edge road well below the picture-reconstructed quay/bridge level. The fixture does not verify elevated urban quay crests,external road grades,original river levels or certified arch clearances. The river rectangle is a separately declared schematic fixture,not an exact bank polygon.",
    "Five existing shared256px graphs provide concrete,sandstone,granite,compact-gravel/asphalt approximation and painted metal;traffic paint uses a palette definition. No private or embedded images. Four browser tiers preserve all five physical openings;near tiers restore finer railings,coursing and paving. Estimated tier errors2/1/.5/.2m are not certified whole-mesh distances. Physical phone/laptop timings and dense-city performance are still unmeasured."
  ],
